// Cloudflare Worker config, pinned on purpose.
//
// Without this file `wrangler deploy` auto-detects the framework, and that
// detection is fragile: adding _config.yml (which GitHub Pages needs, to keep
// the edge function source out of the copy it publishes) made Wrangler decide
// this was a Jekyll site. It set the build command to `npx bundle exec jekyll
// build` — `bundle` is a Ruby tool, not an npm package — and every deploy died
// with "npm error could not determine executable to run" before uploading
// anything. The site silently went stale while main kept moving.
//
// So the settings are declared here instead of guessed. There is NO build step:
// this is hand-written HTML/CSS/JS served straight from the repo root, which is
// what the live site has always done. What must not be published is handled by
// .assetsignore rather than by a build.
{
  "name": "bobcat-bites",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-20",
  "observability": { "enabled": true },
  "assets": {
    // The repo root. index.html, vendor_app.html, the icons, manifests, sw.js
    // and pies/ all sit here, and _headers / _redirects are read from here too.
    "directory": "."
  }
}
